==English==

===Etymology===
Back-formation from {{term/t|en|upholsterer||tradesman who finishes furniture}}, from {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term/t|enm|upholdester}}, from {{term/t|enm|upholder||dealer in small goods}}, from {{term/t|enm|upholden||to repair, uphold}}; see also {{term/t|en|uphold}}.
[[Category:English back-formations]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/əˈpɒl.stə(ɹ)/|/əˈpɐl.stə(ɹ)/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/@"pQl.str@(r)/|/@"p6l.st@(r)/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[fit]] [[padding]], [[stuffing]], [[spring]]s, [[webbing]] and [[fabric]] [[covering]] to [[furniture]].

